!script {{
  --/| ==========================================================================
  --/| Tutorial: Creating D&D 2024 Beacon Repeating Rows
  --/|
  --/| PURPOSE
  --/| This tutorial creates a brand-new NPC Action row on a Beacon character,
  --/| reads the row back, and then removes the temporary row.
  --/|
  --/| HOW TO USE IT
  --/| 1. Select a D&D 2024 Beacon NPC.
  --/| 2. Run this ScriptCard.
  --/| 3. A temporary Action named "ScriptCards Tutorial Action" is created.
  --/| 4. The script reads the new row and removes it before finishing.
  --/|
  --/| CLASSIC SHEETS VS BEACON
  --/| ScriptCards already has an !or command for creating repeating rows.
  --/|
  --/| On a classic sheet, repeating rows are traditional Roll20 Attribute rows.
  --/|
  --/| On Beacon, ScriptCards keeps the same familiar command, but it creates a
  --/| real native Beacon record instead of a collection of fake repeating
  --/| Attribute objects.
  --/|
  --/| HOW SCRIPTSCARDS KNOWS WHAT TO CREATE
  --/| Beacon records contain hidden structural information in addition to fields
  --/| such as name and description.
  --/|
  --/| ScriptCards learns the required shape from a compatible existing record
  --/| and remembers that shape as a creation profile.
  --/|
  --/| If ScriptCards cannot learn a safe structure for that kind of row, it
  --/| refuses the creation rather than guessing.
  --/|
  --/| THE NEW ROW ID
  --/| After a successful creation, SC_LAST_CREATED_ROWID contains the new
  --/| repeating row ID. Save it immediately if the script will need the row.
  --/|
  --/| CLEANUP
  --/| This tutorial creates only a name and description. At the end it deletes
  --/| those two meaningful fields. Once the temporary record is empty,
  --/| ScriptCards removes the canonical Beacon row.
  --/| ==========================================================================

  --#beaconsheet|1
  --#sourcetoken|@{selected|token_id}
  --#title|[*S:npc_name] - Repeating Row Creation Tutorial

  --&CharacterID|[*S:character_id]
  --&CountBefore|[*R:[&CharacterID]:repeating_npcaction:rowcount]

  --+|[c][b]Before Creation[/b][/c]

  --+Section|repeating_npcaction
  --+Rows Before|[&CountBefore]

  --+|[c][b]Create a Native Beacon Action[/b][/c]

  --/| The section can be written as npcaction or repeating_npcaction.
  --!or:[&CharacterID]:npcaction|name:ScriptCards Tutorial Action|description:Temporary row created by the repeating row tutorial

  --/| Save this immediately. The next creation or copy would replace it.
  --&CreatedRowID|[&SC_LAST_CREATED_ROWID]

  --?"[&CreatedRowID]" -eq ""|CreationFailed

  --&CountAfterCreate|[*R:[&CharacterID]:repeating_npcaction:rowcount]

  --Rbysectionid|[&CharacterID];repeating_npcaction;[&CreatedRowID]
  --&CreatedName|[*R:name]
  --&CreatedDescription|[*R:description]

  --+Rows After Creation|[&CountAfterCreate]
  --+New Row ID|[&CreatedRowID]
  --+New Action Name|[&CreatedName]
  --+New Description|[&CreatedDescription]

  --+|[c][b]Remove the Tutorial Row[/b][/c]

  --/| attribute;set with an empty value deletes the named repeating field.
  --/| Removing the last meaningful field lets ScriptCards remove the empty row.
  --~|attribute;set;[&CharacterID];repeating_npcaction_[&CreatedRowID]_description;
  --~|attribute;set;[&CharacterID];repeating_npcaction_[&CreatedRowID]_name;

  --&CountAfterCleanup|[*R:[&CharacterID]:repeating_npcaction:rowcount]

  --+Rows After Cleanup|[&CountAfterCleanup]
  --+Expected Rows|[&CountBefore]

  --+|[c][b]Finished[/b][/c]

  --+Result|A native Beacon Action row was created, read by its new row ID, and removed.
  --X|

  --:CreationFailed|
  --+|[c][b]Creation Could Not Be Completed[/b][/c]
  --+Result|ScriptCards could not learn a compatible native structure for this Action row. No tutorial row was created.
}}
